      <h1 class="jr-h1">Collagen for Joint Pain: What the Research Actually Shows</h1>
      <p class="jr-standfirst">
        Cartilage has no blood supply, which is why joint damage is so slow to repair and why
        what you swallow matters more than it does elsewhere. An orthopaedic surgeon on the
        trials, the doses that worked, and where collagen sits against glucosamine.
      </p>

